Package: speech-dispatcher-vosk
Architecture: any
Depends: speech-dispatcher (>= 0.12~), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: vosk-tts-model-ru-0.9-multi
Description: Speech Dispatcher module for Vosk TTS voices
 Speaks with the neural voices of Vosk TTS (Alpha Cephei) through ONNX
 Runtime, without Python: the Russian multi-speaker model has 5 voices
 (3 female, 2 male) with stress marks from a large dictionary and the
 sentence intonation from a BERT model. The model is loaded into the
 module once and stays loaded.
 Settings in /etc/speech-dispatcher/modules/vosk.conf.

Package: speech-dispatcher-kokoro
Architecture: any
Depends: espeak-ng-data, speech-dispatcher (>= 0.12~), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: kokoro-tts-model-ru, vosk-tts-model-ru-0.9-multi
Description: Speech Dispatcher module for Kokoro voices
 Speaks with Kokoro neural voices through ONNX Runtime, without Python.
 So far Russian (the kokoro-ru model): stress marks from the dictionary of
 Vosk TTS, phonemes from espeak-ng with a dictionary that honours them.
 The model is loaded into the module once and stays loaded.
 Settings in /etc/speech-dispatcher/modules/kokoro.conf.

Package: speech-dispatcher-teratts
Architecture: any
Depends: speech-dispatcher (>= 0.12~), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Recommends: teratts-model-v2, vosk-tts-model-ru-0.9-multi
Description: Speech Dispatcher module for TeraTTSv2 voices
 Speaks with the TeraTTSv2 voices of TeraSpace (Russian and English, 44.1 kHz)
 through ONNX Runtime, without Python. Latin words in Russian text are read
 as English; numbers are spelt out; the Russian stress marks come from the
 dictionary of Vosk TTS. The model is loaded into the module once and stays
 loaded. Settings in /etc/speech-dispatcher/modules/teratts.conf.

Package: speech-dispatcher-sherpa
Architecture: any
# libsherpa-onnx-c-api.so has no versioned soname, so no shlibs entry
Depends: sherpa-onnx (>= 2.0.1), speech-dispatcher (>= 0.12~), ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Speech Dispatcher module for sherpa-onnx voices
 Speaks with the text to speech models of sherpa-onnx through its C API:
 Supertonic, Pocket TTS and VITS models on characters. Models are looked
 up in /usr/share/sherpa-onnx/tts and ~/.local/share/sherpa-onnx/tts; a
 model is loaded into the module once and stays loaded.
 Settings in /etc/speech-dispatcher/modules/sherpa.conf.

Package: speech-dispatcher-silero
Architecture: any
Depends: python3,
         python3-num2words,
         python3-numpy,
         python3-onnxruntime,
         speech-dispatcher (>= 0.12~),
         ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends}
Description: Speech Dispatcher module for Silero TTS (Russian)
 Speaks with the neural Silero voices (v5_6_ru: aidar, baya, eugene,
 kseniya, xenia). The model runs in a resident silero-server (ONNX Runtime,
 CPU), loaded once; it survives speech-dispatcher reloads and stops after an
 hour without speech. Settings in /etc/speech-dispatcher/modules/silero.conf.
 .
 The model and its runtime are licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (non-commercial use
 only) and are not part of this package; install them, with their licences,
 into ~/.local/share/silero-tts/v5_6_ru.
